// PlayerModelLib resolves attribute descriptions by first checking for a
// value-suffixed key "charattribute-{attr}-{value}", then falling back to
// "charattribute-{attr}" as a format string filled with the value. The
// format-string fallback throws (confirmed in client-main.log: "Translation
// string format exception thrown for: '{0:P0} armor walk speed penalty'")
// with the installed PlayerModelLib version, so this file uses value-suffixed
// keys exclusively, matching the installed racialability mod's own working
// lang file (assets/game/lang/en.json inside racialability_*.zip).
// Known tradeoff: these keys break silently (render nothing, no exception) if
// a trait's numeric value in traits.json changes without updating the
// matching key here — when you change a trait value, update its key too.
// Where a value could plausibly be formatted with or without a trailing zero
// (e.g. 0.10 vs 0.1), both key forms are included defensively, mirroring
// racialability's own file, which does the same for the same reason.
